PRO-FORMA FIRST BOARD OF DIRECTORS RESOLUTION OF [CN_WFOE_LTD], A WHOLLY FOREIGN-OWNED LIMITED LIABILITY COMPANY INCORPORATED UNDER THE LAWS OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA.
WHEREAS, the subscribers have procured the formation of CN_WFOE_LTD (the Company), a wholly foreign-owned limited liability company, under the Company Law of the People's Republic of China, the Foreign Investment Law of the People's Republic of China, and all applicable registration regulations;
WHEREAS, the Company has adopted Articles of Association setting forth its corporate name, registered office, object and scope of business, authorized share capital, shareholder, directors, supervisor, management, financial powers, duration, and dissolution procedures;
WHEREAS, the sole foreign shareholder has subscribed for the entire issued share capital of the Company and has agreed to contribute such capital in accordance with the capital contribution schedule contained in the Articles of Association;
WHEREAS, the Board of Directors recognizes the necessity of adopting first resolutions to confirm the capital subscription, adopt the registered office, authorize banking arrangements, and appoint statutory officers;
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED AS FOLLOWS:
1. Share Capital Subscription. The Board accepts and confirms the subscription in full of the registered capital by the sole shareholder. Management is directed to record the subscribed capital in the company's books, issue any capital contribution certificate or share certificate as required by the Articles of Association, and open the necessary capital account for the receipt of paid-in contributions. The Board approves the five-year contribution schedule and directs that all contributions be funded in accordance with the Foreign Investment Law and foreign exchange administration rules.
2. Registered Office Adoption. The Board adopts the registered office at the address to be stated in the Business License and Articles of Association in China as the Company's statutory seat, registered address, and principal place of management. The Board authorizes the legal representative to execute a lease agreement, obtain title or use-right documentation, and file any change or confirmation required by the local Market Supervision Administration.
3. Banking Authorization. The Board appoints the bank designated in the opening forms as the Company's principal banker and authorizes the opening of basic deposit, general deposit, foreign currency capital, and RMB capital accounts. The legal representative, general manager, and designated finance manager are authorized, individually or jointly as determined by management, to execute banking mandates, sign account opening documents, and operate the accounts subject to internal expenditure approval limits established by the Articles of Association.
4. Statutory Officer Appointments. The Board ratifies and appoints the individual named as executive director and legal representative, the individual named as general manager, and the individual named as supervisor, each with the powers and duties prescribed by the Company Law and Articles of Association. The legal representative is authorized to execute all statutory filings, tax registrations, foreign investment information reports, labor registrations, and any other instruments necessary for the Company's lawful operation.
5. Ratification and Further Action. The Board ratifies all acts already performed in connection with incorporation and directs each officer, director, and authorized agent to execute documents, make filings, and take actions as may be necessary to give full effect to these resolutions. These resolutions may be executed in counterparts and shall be effective immediately.
